#: d0fd1b9d0ecd4621bf4d87ffb35ac3a4
msgid "**Using all capital letters**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/rst-documentation-style-guide.rst:744
#: 71d04edee70544369106b534b3d938df
msgid ""
"We have observed that many novices make the mistake of typing the "
"surrounding angled brackets (``< >``) on the command line, even after "
"substituting the desired real value between them. Therefore, in "
"documentation aimed at novices, we also recommend clarifying that the angled "
"brackets should not be typed. This can be accomplished in one of several "
"ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/rst-documentation-style-guide.rst:746
#: cb26d8728c654f63b8263ab3a59e367d
msgid "**Explicitly say something like \"without the angled brackets\".**"
